ud passes over  the Sun then Luke vanishes leaving  behind just his robes becoming one with  the force in the same way that obi-wan  vanished when Darth Vader struck him  down in a new hope and also how Yoda  passed away in Return of the Jedi Luke  sacrificed to save the resistance  allowing them to escape the first order  also mirrors obi-wan sacrifice which  allowed Han Leia and Luke to escape  Vader this is a heartbreaking scene for  many fans but there's some important  visual symbolism here to Luke's  sacrifice brought some balance back as  the first order was about to snuff out  the resistance before his intervention  and the cloud partially obscuring the  Sun suggests the light and the darkness  in some sort of balance at one point in  the sequence what looked like a faint  rainbow appeared in the sky not only can  rainbows be a sign of hope change in a  bridge between worlds was also in the  Buddhist tradition a rainbow body as a  state of enlightenment when a person  achieves the highest  of meditation and complete knowledge and  is often said to happen around the time  of death with the body dissolving into  light the Jedi way and Star Wars borrows  from various Eastern traditions and  philosophies one of which is Buddhism so  I think the rainbow symbolism goes  perfectly with the idea of Luke having  reached a higher state with his ability  to force project himself and then when  he becomes one with the force at the end  later in the scene we also see two sons  on the horizon which is another  nostalgic call back to when Luke walked  out on Tatooine in a new hope and looked  out over the sunset I'm pretty sure Luke  will return in episode 9 though most  likely as a force ghost with an ongoing  ability to participate and influence  events Yoda already came back as a force  ghost in the last Jedi and set the  forestry on fire and I think we could  see Luke have new scenes with Rey and  kylo in the next movie after all his  parting words to kylo were see you