race the dark  side throughout the last Jedi he is  still conflicted for example hesitating  to kill his mother Leia and I wonder if  given that Luke told layer no one's ever  really gone we may see kylo redeem  himself in some way by the end of  episode 9 as Darth Vader did by the end  of Return of the Jedi though if this did  happen I'd expect that to be a spin on  it to make it at least a bit different  of course Luke's line that no one's ever  really gone also refers to Han Solo and  Luke hands Leia the dice from the  Millennium Falcon just after saying this  but Luke's words also foreshadow his own  sacrifice at the end of the movie and  his likely return in episode 9 before we  leave crate we need to talk about Finn  and rose in contrast to his attempt to  lead the resistance early on in the film  Finn ends up willing to sacrifice  himself with a cause when he speeds  towards the first orders mega cannon and  although I never really believed that  Episode eight would be the end for Finn  director Rian Johnson did manage to rack  up the tension but Rose drops in  literally crashing his speeder off  course and then unexpectedly kisses him  it's interesting that Finn and roses  last major scene together calls back to  their first scene which also featured  Rose scuffering Finn's plans when she  stopped him leaving in an escape pod but  a lots changed since then and finis  stepped up proving worthy of roses high  opinion of him as a hero and Rose  herself as proven worthy of the title  hero as well and roses line to Finn that  they should win by saving what they love  not by fighting what they hate was a  positive moment amid a bleak situation  for the resistance and echos what Luke  was taught by Yoda and obi-wan about not  giving in to hate I wasn't necessarily  expecting the movie to pair up Rose and  Finn but given they did it's a nice  touch that she ends a film healing up  similar to how fin finished his story in  the force awakens so those were the  final scenes with the main cast but just  before the credits roll we get an  important short scene set back on Kanto  bite where we see the stable hands  reenacting the events on crate with  their own handmade toys the scene shows  that news and stories of how the  legendary Jedi Master stood up to kylo  Ren in the first order have spread  through the galaxy  reigniting a spark that will light the  fire to burn the first order down as PO  dam run says at the end of the movie in  an echo vice-admiral hold those words  one of the boys then goes outside and as  he's force-sensitive he calls a broom to  him then looks up and sees a streak of  light flash across the sky we can then  see that he's wearing the old rebellion  ring that Rose Tico gave him earlier in  the movie it's a moment filled with hope  and confirms Luke's claim to kylo Ren  that the rebellion is reborn by the way  according to the visual dictionary the  boy's name appears to be tamiri black  and I wonder whether he will actually be  a specific new force user who will  appear in either episode 9 or the new  trilogy that Rian Johnson's developing  after JJ Abrams film if he is going to  appear again then we may well revisit  canto bite in a future movie also I  think it's intriguing that this boy like  Rey has been sold and abandoned by his  parents which means we're guessing a  theme in Star Wars that a force user  doesn't always need to inherit their  force abilities from a special or  privileged family this scene also hints  that we may get a time jump between the  end of the last Jedi in episode 9  this would allow time for stories to  spread about Luke Skywalker and the  resistance and how they foiled the first  order a time gap could also be a  possible way to deal with Leia's story  in episode 9 and the fact that Carrie  Fisher is so sadly no longer with us and  if you're interested in my thoughts and  theories on how I think we'll see layers  are completed in the sequel then tap in  the top right or check the video  description for my Carrie Fisher video  so what did you think about the last  Jedi and did it live up to your  expectations and do you have any  predictions on what you think we'll see  in episode 9  leave me a comment below and be sure to  subscribe to end my Star Wars giveaway  for a very cool last Jedi Funko pop the  winner of my latest superhero giveaway  is on screen right now so if that's you  send me a private message so I can get  your prize out to you coming up I've got  more last Jedi videos so turn on  notifications to get them as soon as I  upload them and in the means  you can check out some more videos  you're sure to like right here thanks  for watching and see you next time you  became movie lovers
 

